      "text": "Mosk pointed at the door, his eyes narrow and sharp. Lina wondered if sneaking past would be safer, but her heart urged her to offer the last apple of the season instead. She set the fruit on the step, hoping the gesture might soften the grumpy fox. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his tail twitching. Finally, he stood up, tied his vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word, leaving the apple behind."
