{
  "bridge_text": "The old fox Mosk watched her with eyes like polished amber, waiting for her to turn back. With his patched green vest tucked tight, the story continues deeper into the hollow tree.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow trunk, Lina discovered a spiral of stairs winding downward. Perched on the very top step sat an old, grey fox wearing a small, patched green vest. This was Mosk. His voice sounded like dry leaves skittering on stone as he warned Lina that the tree was no place for visitors. He insisted she go home and forget the humming, but Lina stood firm, telling the fox she could not possibly forget a sound she had not yet heard."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
