{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's light flickers like a dying ember as Mosk watches, his heart heavy with the weight of that long-ago winter. Let us see if they can mend what was broken.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The firefly's golden light dimmed, pulsing slowly like a fading star against the mossy floor. Mosk stood frozen, his whiskers twitching as he remembered that bitter winter when he had missed his chance to help. He had guarded this hollow tree ever since, keeping his distance, not knowing if he could ever make amends for his mistake."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt softly and asked the firefly queen what she needed to feel strong again. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, the queen whispered, for that was all the medicine she ever truly required. Mosk hurried to fetch milk in a tiny thimble, laying his paw gently beside hers. As the queen's glow steadied, the tree began to hum a new, hopeful tune, and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

